Schelm
======

Schelm is an independent compiler distribution maintained by the Schelm
contributors. It is based on the Lamdera compiler, which is in turn derived
from the Elm compiler.

Elm compiler copyright 2012-present Evan Czaplicki.
Lamdera compiler copyright 2020-present Mario Rogic.

The Elm and Lamdera names identify upstream projects. Neither Evan Czaplicki,
Mario Rogic, the Elm project, nor the Lamdera project endorses Schelm.

The complete BSD-3-Clause terms are in LICENSE. Source distributions must keep
LICENSE and this attribution. Binary distributions must reproduce the license,
copyright notices, disclaimer, and this attribution in their accompanying
materials.
